            "Stripped out the legacy custom authentication layer that had accumulated 3 years of patches and replaced it with Better Auth. The new system supports Google and GitHub OAuth, email magic links with 5-minute expiry, and a comprehensive role-based access control model with four tiers: owner, admin, member, and viewer. Session management uses 7-day tokens with 24-hour sliding window refresh. Rate limiting is enforced at the IP level with 10 sign-in attempts per 15-minute window. The migration preserved all existing user accounts with zero downtime by running a shadow auth system in parallel for 48 hours before cutover. Password hashes were migrated using bcrypt compatibility mode.",
            "completed", "Security", "Marcus Chen", "4 weeks",
            ["Auth", "Security", "OAuth", "RBAC"],
            "Zero auth-related incidents since launch"),
        new("e3", "Feb 24, 2026", "Design system v2.0 shipped",
            "40 components with full a11y support, dark mode, and Storybook docs.",
            "Launched version 2.0 of the internal design system with 40 production-ready components built on Radix UI primitives. Every component passes WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards with comprehensive keyboard navigation, screen reader announcements, and focus management. The token system uses CSS custom properties with semantic naming, enabling runtime theme switching between light and dark modes with zero flash. Each component has an interactive Storybook story showing all variants, props, and usage examples. The design system is published as an internal npm package with semantic versioning and automated changelog generation. Adoption across the three product teams reached 92% within two weeks of launch.",
            "completed", "Design", "Priya Patel", "5 weeks",
            ["Design System", "Components", "A11y", "Storybook"],
            "92% team adoption, 60% faster UI development"),
        new("e4", "Mar 10, 2026", "Real-time collaboration engine",
            "WebSocket presence with CRDT sync for concurrent editing.",
            "Building the real-time collaboration layer on top of Yjs CRDT with a custom WebSocket provider hosted on Cloudflare Durable Objects. The system supports real-time cursor positions with user avatars, text selection highlighting across participants, and per-user undo/redo stacks that do not interfere with each other. The server handles up to 500 concurrent connections per workspace with automatic reconnection using exponential backoff and an offline operation queue that replays when connectivity returns. Current benchmarks show changes syncing within 50ms on stable connections and conflict resolution handling correctly even with 200ms simulated network delay. The awareness protocol broadcasts user presence, active document, and idle status to all workspace members.",
            "current", "Engineering", "Jordan Liu", "3 weeks in",
            ["WebSocket", "CRDT", "Yjs", "Real-time"],
            "Targeting 50ms sync latency at scale"),
        new("e5", "Apr 2026", "Performance optimization sprint",
            "Lighthouse 95+, bundle reduction, and edge caching strategy.",
            "Planned optimization sprint focused on three pillars: frontend bundle size reduction through code splitting and tree shaking, server response time improvement through edge caching with Vercel ISR, and Core Web Vitals optimization targeting LCP under 1.2s, FID under 50ms, and CLS under 0.05. The bundle analysis identified 340KB of unused polyfills and 180KB of duplicate lodash imports that can be eliminated. Edge caching will be implemented for all read-heavy API routes with a 60-second stale-while-revalidate strategy. Image optimization will switch to AVIF with WebP fallback, reducing total image payload by an estimated 45%. The goal is Lighthouse performance score of 95+ on all public-facing pages.",
            "upcoming", "Performance", "Team", "3 weeks planned",
            ["Lighthouse", "Bundle", "Caching", "CWV"],
            "Target: 95+ Lighthouse, sub-1.2s LCP"),
        new("e6", "May 2026", "Public beta launch",
            "Waitlist rollout with onboarding wizard and in-app feedback.",
            "The public beta will open access to the first 2,000 waitlist members over 4 weeks, ramping from 100 to 500 invites per week. The onboarding flow includes workspace creation, team invitation via email, template gallery selection, and a 5-step interactive product tour highlighting key features. In-app feedback collection will use contextual NPS prompts at key moments: after first workspace creation, after first team collaboration session, and at the 7-day mark. A dedicated Slack community will provide direct access to the product team for real-time feedback during the beta period.",
            "upcoming", "Launch", "Team", "4 weeks planned",
            ["Beta", "Onboarding", "Waitlist", "Feedback"],
            "Target: 2,000 beta users, 40%+ activation"),
    ];

    private string _selectedId = "e4";

    private static string StatusDotClass(string status) => status switch
    {
        "completed" => "border-emerald-500 bg-emerald-500",
        "current" => "border-blue-500 bg-blue-500",
        _ => "border-muted-foreground/30 bg-transparent",
    };

    private static string LineColorClass(string status) => status switch
    {
        "completed" => "bg-emerald-500/30",
        "current" => "bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-500/30 to-muted-foreground/15",
        _ => "bg-muted-foreground/15",
    };
}
